  "history_summaries": [
    "Repair round 1/3: Replaced all 5 broken assertImpliesDelay calls with equivalent fvAssert-based manual implication+delay. Root cause: assertImpliesDelay in chiselFv generates incorrect SVA (loses antecedent and delay range, producing unconditional assertions). Fix: (1) sA_to_sC_in_2_cycles: 2-deep pipeline of antecedent+consequent, checks if sA at t-2 implies sC at t-2/t-1/t (##[0:2]); (2) steady_state_sC: RegNext-delayed antecedent checks ##[1]; (3) shift_reg_1_to_2 through shift_reg_3_to_4: RegNext-delayed sC-antecedent checks ##[1] shift-register integrity. All original assertion labels preserved. Homologous shift-register assertions all repaired identically.",
    "Repair round 2/3: Fixed spurious CEX in `sA_to_sC_in_2_cycles` by initializing assertion pipeline registers with `false.B` reset values. Root cause: `RegNext` used without init values allows the formal solver to pick arbitrary initial register values, creating a false counterexample where `a_sA_d2=1` (uninitialized) and all `c_sC` variants=0 (stato stuck at sA with no clock edge). Fix changed lines 144-146: `RegNext(RegNext(a_sA))` → `RegNext(RegNext(a_sA, false.B), false.B)`, `RegNext(RegNext(c_sC))` → `RegNext(RegNext(c_sC, false.B), false.B)`, `RegNext(c_sC)` → `RegNext(c_sC, false.B)`. After reset all pipeline registers start at false.B, making the implication antecedent false and the assertion vacuously true until valid history accumulates. Label `sA_to_sC_in_2_cycles` preserved. No homologous assertions with 2-deep RegNext pipeline exist; the other assertions use 1-deep `RegNext` which is structurally distinct."
  ],
